<title>SINGAPORE: ST Electronic &amp; Engineering net up 44.5.</title>
<headline>ST Electronic &amp; Engineering net up 44.5.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				7.28 vs   5.04</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)		   12.00 vs  10.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		     0.12 vs   0.08</p>
<p>    Turnover				152.12 vs 127.26</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	 2.51 vs   1.70</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    0.09 vs   0.29</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)		5.45 vs   4.80</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	     0.33 vs   0.13</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 10.75 vs   7.60</p>
<p>    Tax					 3.13 vs   2.43</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries			 nil  vs   0.35 (gain)</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:		    July 3, 1997</p>
<p>    Last day books open:		  June 23, 1997</p>
<p>Note - ST Electronic &amp; Engineering Ltd is involved in electronic systems integration and related businesses.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
